From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <mk@verveflux.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Feb 2026 17:54:53 +0530
Subject: Migrate override storage from Symbol to V8 Private, add preload
 registration bridge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the visible Symbol.for('__co') override container with a V8 Private
property (kCustomOverridesPrivateKey). V8 Private properties are completely
invisible to JavaScript reflection (Object.getOwnPropertyNames/Symbols,
Reflect.ownKeys, for...in, Proxy traps), making the override mechanism
undetectable by web content.

Key changes:

custom_override_helpers.h:
- Define kCustomOverridesPrivateKey ("__co_private") constant
- GetCustomOverrideFunction now reads from global.GetPrivate() instead
  of global.Get(Symbol.for('__co'))

v8_builtin_overrides.cc:
- Add shared helpers: GetPrivateOverrideContainer,
  GetOrCreatePrivateOverrideContainer, LookupOverrideFromPrivate
- Refactor GenericBuiltinWrapper, GenericConstructorWrapper,
  OverridePropertyAccessorGetter, OverrideDataPropertyGetter,
  GenericOverrideOnlyCallback, and InstallPropertyExistenceOverrides
  to use the new Private-based lookup helpers (removes ~120 lines of
  duplicated Symbol lookup boilerplate)
- Add preload registration bridge functions:
  __ro(iface, name, fn)  — register override function
  __rov(iface, name, val) — register override value (e.g. arrays)
  __rUA(data) — set UA override data via NavigatorUAData::setUA(),
  self-destructs after first call
- InstallOverrideRegistrationBridge installs these as non-enumerable,
  configurable properties on the global; preload scripts call them to
  populate the Private container, then delete them when done

navigator_ua_data.idl:
- Remove setUA() from the web-exposed IDL surface; it is now called
  exclusively via the __rUA C++ bridge function, preventing web content
  from detecting or calling it

